@file 18:
@@file 19: read_io_file -no_die_size_adjust pad.io  
Reading IO assignment file "pad.io" ...
@file 20:
@file 21: source floorplan.tcl
#@ Begin verbose source floorplan.tcl (pre)
@file 1:
@@file 2: set_db [get_db base_cells -if {.class == core}] .symmetry xy ;
@file 2: # Issue with stdcells not having symmetry in lef files, forced xy to fix this. (NOT a nice solution) /KW
@file 3:
@file 4: # Set design attributes
@@file 5: set_db design_process_node 65
##  Process: 65            (User Set)               
##     Node: (not set)                           

##  Check design process and node:  
##  Design tech node is not set.

Applying the recommended capacitance filtering threshold values for 65nm process node: total_c_th=0, relative_c_th=1 and coupling_c_th=0.1.
	These values will be used by all post-route extraction engines, including TQuantus, IQuantus and Quantus QRC extraction.
	Capacitance filtering mode(extract_rc_cap_filter_mode option of the set_db) is 'relative_and_coupling' for all engines.
	The accuracy mode for post_route extract_rc_effort_level low extraction will be set to 'high'.
	Default value for EffortLevel(extract_rc_effort_level option of the set_db) in post_route extraction mode is 'medium'.
@file 6:
@@file 7: set_db design_top_routing_layer M7
@@file 8: set_db design_bottom_routing_layer M2 
@@file 9: set_db design_flow_effort standard ;
@file 9: # {express standard extreme}
@@file 10: set_db design_power_effort low ;
@file 10: # {none low high}
@file 11:
@file 12: # Set timing attributes
@@file 13: set_db timing_analysis_cppr           both
@@file 14: set_db timing_analysis_type           ocv
@file 15:
@file 16:
@@file 17: set_preference CmdLogMode 2 ;
@file 18:
@file 19:
@file 20:
@file 21: #core size
@file 22: set core_dx [expr [get_db [lindex [get_db insts -if {.name == *sram*}] 0] .bbox.dx] * 11] ;
@file 23: set core_dy 1410 ;
@@file 24: create_floorplan -site CORE -core_size $core_dx $core_dy 40 40 40 40
Start create_tracks
